WEBVTT

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:12.250
The target is gone and the earth is saved.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.083
Thanks for all your hard work this past year.

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:19.333
I imagine there are some things
you'll find hard to swallow.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:22.708
You'll have all eyes on you
for a while, I'm afraid,

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:25.958
and I'm sure they'll be asking
to keep mum on confidential matters.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:29.750
I'll do my utmost to protect you, of course,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.375
but allow me to apologize in advance.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.417
Mr. Karasuma, it's fine.

00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:42.250
We'll do our best to
get this settled peacefully, too.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.375
We don't want to complicate things for you.

00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:48.583
In return, we <i>do </i>have one request.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.250
Please let us attend Kunugigaoka's
graduation ceremony today.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.625
Our days spent battling with the main campus

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:59.875
are yet another precious memory
we made with Koro Sensei.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:06.917
Sure--I'll arrange it.
After all, that's why I'm here.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.292
All students: stand up!

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.417
Mr. Karasuma, Professor Bitch--
you taught us so much. Thank you!

00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.792
Thank you!

00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:29.375
So where <i>is </i>graduation, anyway?

00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:33.083
School's locked up tight.
Looks like it's at the civic center.

00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:35.875
We'll need our folks to bring by our uniforms.

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:42.458
There must still be some
lingering sadness, and yet...

00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:44.458
How strong they've become--

00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:47.042
they're almost unrecognizable from a year ago.

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:55.792
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:55.792 --> 00:01:58.792
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:58.792 --> 00:02:01.250
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.042
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:06.583
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.292
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:14.542
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:02:14.542 --> 00:02:20.625
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:25.167
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:31.292
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:02:31.292 --> 00:02:35.917
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:37.458
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:43.458
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:46.542
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:48.083
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:52.167
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:57.167
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.667
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:00.125
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:03:00.125 --> 00:03:02.750
"Congratulations on your graduation!"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.250
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.083
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:03:17.917 --> 00:03:21.917
"25th Period: Future Time"
"by Kaede Kayano & Nagisa Shiota"

00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:31.542
"Kunugigaoka Junior High Graduation Ceremony"

00:03:31.542 --> 00:03:32.875
"Kunugigaoka Junior High Graduation Ceremony"
Koro Sensei never said anything about the E-Class system being wrong

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:36.750
Koro Sensei never said anything about the E-Class system being wrong

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.917
or that we would try to get it changed.

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:41.417
--Hinano Kurahashi.
--Sir!

00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:44.833
This world is full of absurdities
as a matter of course.

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:48.292
If you have the time to be
resentful and resigned to that...

00:03:48.292 --> 00:03:50.292
Nagisa Shiota!

00:03:50.292 --> 00:03:52.667
Sir!

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:55.333
...have fun fighting those absurdities instead.

00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:58.792
He taught us plenty of ways to do it, too.

00:03:59.542 --> 00:04:02.750
You've got a sharp look
in your eyes these days.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.875
The result of your
teacher's instruction, I'm sure.

00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:10.333
Yes, sir. And please don't overdo things.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.042
Take care, now.

00:04:20.958 --> 00:04:22.833
That was a nice ceremony, wasn't it?

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.750
--I was really moved!
--Right?

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.917
Huh?!

00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:32.625
Mom, Dad... Why are you here together?

00:04:32.625 --> 00:04:34.458
At the end of last month,

00:04:34.458 --> 00:04:39.125
that monster--your teacher--paid me a visit.

00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:43.333
Nagisa asked me a favor at the very start:

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:47.917
He wants to be called
by his first name, not his last.

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:51.000
That way, he says, there'll be
no discomfort calling on him

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.917
even if he goes back to using his father's name.

00:04:54.917 --> 00:04:57.833
He's a fine child. No complaints.

00:04:57.833 --> 00:05:02.417
He's likely to meet
his major goals by mid-March.

00:05:02.417 --> 00:05:07.333
Please give him your blessing--as a family.

00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:11.333
Both he and your mother
told me how hard you worked,

00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:15.083
how determined you were in making it this far.

00:05:15.083 --> 00:05:19.000
Your father and I have talked it over.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.333
We'll follow your example
and work hard to give us another try.

00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:25.792
Huh?

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:36.750
Just how much of himself
did our teacher need to leave behind?

00:05:38.917 --> 00:05:40.792
The ceremony's over!

00:05:40.792 --> 00:05:42.667
It's interview time!

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.917
--E Class, a word?
--This place is off limits!

00:05:45.917 --> 00:05:48.375
Tell us about the monster!

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:50.208
How do you feel right now?

00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:52.250
Did you really kill him?

00:05:52.917 --> 00:05:54.958
Hey, buddy, outta the way!

00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:59.208
You vultures! Spare a thought
for the students' feelings for once!

00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:00.500
Who cares?!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.417
Outside, everyone--quickly!

00:06:02.417 --> 00:06:04.875
There's a bus standing by
outside the main gate!

00:06:04.875 --> 00:06:06.042
Hey! Ow!

00:06:06.042 --> 00:06:07.500
What the--?!

00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:10.625
"Kunugigaoka"

00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:14.958
What the hell are you doing?

00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:17.000
Quit meddling with our coverage!

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:22.375
<i>You </i>quit meddling with our moment in the sun!

00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:25.417
After a little editing,
I might just release this online!

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:27.625
We know what you look like!

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:34.333
Now let us escort you to the front gate.

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:38.292
Our ties and our relationship
end today, for the most part,

00:06:38.292 --> 00:06:41.833
but we <i>are </i>still students
who studied at the same school.

00:06:41.833 --> 00:06:46.250
To abandon you now would
bring shame upon your ruler--me.

00:06:49.792 --> 00:06:51.542
Akabane?

00:06:51.542 --> 00:06:54.333
Seems you're the only one staying on.

00:06:54.333 --> 00:06:58.958
Once all this blows over, I'll string you up
and make you spill the beans...

00:06:58.958 --> 00:07:01.500
You'll tell me about this Koro Sensei guy

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.292
who actually managed to get you all this far.

00:07:04.292 --> 00:07:06.000
Sure, I don't mind.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.208
But with your hard head,
you might struggle to understand it all.

00:07:10.208 --> 00:07:13.125
--C'mon, you're bringing up the rear.
--Whoa!

00:07:15.375 --> 00:07:17.167
Off you go.

00:07:36.958 --> 00:07:39.750
A day like today,
with so many reasons for tears...

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.917
I doubt I'll see another like it.

00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:53.250
Goodbye, Kunugigaoka Junior High.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:57.000
Goodbye, Class 3-E.

00:07:58.958 --> 00:07:59.708
Goodbye...

00:07:59.708 --> 00:08:01.625
<i>Ah, up here on this hill</i>
Goodbye...

00:08:01.625 --> 00:08:03.625
<i>Ah, up here on this hill</i>
...Koro Sensei.

00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:06.667
<i>Ah, up here on this hill</i>

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:11.042
<i>Farewells come around</i>
<i>  </i>

00:08:11.042 --> 00:08:13.708
<i>The jet contrails that held our hopes</i>
<i>  </i>

00:08:13.708 --> 00:08:17.625
<i>The jet contrails that held our hopes</i>
Lots of stuff happened after that.

00:08:17.625 --> 00:08:19.500
Kunugigaoka Academy came under fire

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.292
for putting its students in harm's way.

00:08:20.292 --> 00:08:23.625
"Keep Out" "No Trespassing"
for putting its students in harm's way.

00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:24.833
"Keep Out" "No Trespassing"
The E-Class system, too,

00:08:24.833 --> 00:08:27.458
"Keep Out" "No Trespassing"
was seen as problematic and abolished.

00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:32.667
"Keep Out" "No Trespassing"
After we left, the E Class campus closed its doors for good.

00:08:33.625 --> 00:08:40.500
The principal had to
relinquish his administrative rights.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:45.750
But I get the feeling he would
already have accounted for that.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.833
He's a man of tough convictions and prodigious wit.

00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:50.292
"Ten Years at Kunugigaoka"
He's a man of tough convictions and prodigious wit.

00:08:50.292 --> 00:08:54.458
"Ten Years at Kunugigaoka"
I'm sure he'll be working in education again somewhere soon.

00:08:54.458 --> 00:08:55.667
"Ten Years at Kunugigaoka"

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:58.708
"Ten Years at Kunugigaoka"
Can we help, Mr. Asano?

00:09:00.917 --> 00:09:05.125
Ah, Nagai and Mori!
How many years has it been?

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.167
We heard things were really rough.

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:14.833
Both for you and for
the students who came after us.

00:09:14.833 --> 00:09:17.792
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:09:17.792 --> 00:09:20.417
If we can be of any use to our mentor...

00:09:23.917 --> 00:09:27.583
Well, let's see. Can I ask you one favor, then?

00:09:29.625 --> 00:09:37.125
Will you celebrate this new start
for me and your juniors?

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:40.167
Come, let's drink.
We'll talk about what you're doing now

00:09:40.167 --> 00:09:42.292
and I'll air out my complaints.

00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:47.000
We'll listen to anything you have to say.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.958
All three of us.

00:09:51.708 --> 00:09:59.500
The thirty-billion-yen bounty
was promptly paid out.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:05.875
Like Mr. Karasuma said,
it was hush money, too, of a sort.

00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:08.125
We talked it over.

00:10:08.125 --> 00:10:11.083
After referring to Koro Sensei's book of advice...

00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:11.417
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"
After referring to Koro Sensei's book of advice...

00:10:11.417 --> 00:10:14.083
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"
The accomplishment's the thing!

00:10:14.083 --> 00:10:15.958
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"
You can't grow up right if you live your life

00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:18.292
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"
relying on scads of money!

00:10:18.292 --> 00:10:19.875
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"
And so...

00:10:19.875 --> 00:10:21.875
...we each took some
as a down payment for tuition

00:10:21.875 --> 00:10:24.792
and for living on our own,

00:10:24.792 --> 00:10:28.208
donated here and there to various places,

00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:32.750
then made one big-ticket purchase together.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:39.000
The rest we returned to the government
in thanks for their year of support.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:45.250
Mr. Karasuma--<i>Agent </i>Karasuma's
reputation is sure to rise.

00:10:47.375 --> 00:10:51.625
The moon began to crumble, slowly but surely.

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:54.958
Under its own gravity,
it would eventually end up

00:10:54.958 --> 00:10:57.958
a much smaller sphere than before.

00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:02.542
The explosion had also
brought it closer to Earth,

00:11:02.542 --> 00:11:06.708
so after a while, its size,
shape, gravity and orbit

00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:09.792
would start to look and feel
very similar to the way it was

00:11:09.792 --> 00:11:12.250
before its destruction.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.542
The crescent moon
that symbolized our year together

00:11:18.542 --> 00:11:22.250
would slowly forget its shape.

00:11:25.875 --> 00:11:29.875
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:11:37.375 --> 00:11:38.292
"Ministry of Defense"

00:11:38.292 --> 00:11:41.083
"Ministry of Defense"
There's been some dangerous movement from an organization

00:11:41.083 --> 00:11:43.542
"Ministry of Defense"
that incites violence in the Middle East.

00:11:43.542 --> 00:11:48.500
The plan is to send in a secret agent
to infiltrate their group.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.583
You'll head there tomorrow, Irina.

00:11:51.583 --> 00:11:54.875
Okay, sure...

00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:58.167
But I'm scared, Chief Karasuma.

00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:04.125
If a gorgeous woman like me
gets captured in dangerous territory...

00:12:04.125 --> 00:12:06.208
Or does that turn you on?

00:12:06.208 --> 00:12:12.000
Picturing your wife having
all kinds of things done to her...

00:12:12.875 --> 00:12:16.583
I asked you to go because
I had faith in your abilities.

00:12:16.583 --> 00:12:20.458
But if that's really how you see yourself...

00:12:20.458 --> 00:12:24.000
Then I have no choice. I'll ask someone else.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.083
Huh? But--

00:12:25.083 --> 00:12:29.250
I was joking! I just wanted you
to show a little concern!

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:32.167
Come <i>on</i>, sweetie!

00:12:32.167 --> 00:12:33.542
So you're going?

00:12:33.542 --> 00:12:35.083
I'm going!

00:12:35.083 --> 00:12:36.458
Then go get ready!

00:12:36.458 --> 00:12:39.083
Yes, sir! Gladly!

00:12:42.458 --> 00:12:46.000
It's been seven years since we met...

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.125
...and she hasn't changed a bit.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.458
I wonder if my and her--

00:12:52.458 --> 00:12:53.708
"Kunugigaoka Station"
I wonder if my and her--

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.875
and his students are doing all right?

00:12:57.875 --> 00:13:01.375
"Morning TV Drama" "Dragonfly"
and his students are doing all right?

00:13:01.375 --> 00:13:03.375
and his students are doing all right?

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:07.000
"Old Campus"

00:13:17.917 --> 00:13:20.667
Hey-hey, Miss TV Drama Actress!

00:13:20.667 --> 00:13:22.167
Hi, everyone!

00:13:26.917 --> 00:13:31.333
Kaede, are you in costume?
Are you sure you're not too busy?

00:13:31.333 --> 00:13:34.000
I sneaked out on a break.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.542
I can't always let you guys do all the work.

00:13:37.542 --> 00:13:39.208
All right...

00:13:39.208 --> 00:13:42.375
Okay, folks--let's start
taking care of this place!

00:13:42.375 --> 00:13:44.333
Yeah! Let's do it!

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:47.167
Once class president, always class president!

00:13:47.167 --> 00:13:50.625
Well, you all practically
forced me to hold on to the key!

00:13:50.625 --> 00:13:55.375
This kind of stuff has
always been best left to you.

00:14:09.208 --> 00:14:12.333
Hey, are you done reading
"Koro Sensei's Rules to Live By"?

00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:15.083
Nowhere near! It never ends.

00:14:15.083 --> 00:14:17.375
It's getting a little
rough around the edges again.

00:14:17.375 --> 00:14:20.083
And we bought this mountain, too...

00:14:20.083 --> 00:14:22.875
It's okay. If you mess it up, clean it up--

00:14:22.875 --> 00:14:25.125
that's one of our school rules.

00:14:25.125 --> 00:14:29.125
Boy, have <i>you </i>hit the big time, Kayano.

00:14:29.125 --> 00:14:33.333
Well, geez--she's got the looks,
she can handle action,

00:14:33.333 --> 00:14:36.292
and she can jump off
a thirty-meter cliff with a smile.

00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:38.042
It'd be weirder if she <i>weren't </i>so big.

00:14:38.042 --> 00:14:41.583
No, no--I'm just relying
on my legacy from junior high.

00:14:41.583 --> 00:14:46.292
And Okajima, quit the
low-angle shots and get to work.

00:14:47.333 --> 00:14:51.125
We agreed that we didn't need a grave.

00:14:52.792 --> 00:14:54.417
After all...

00:14:54.417 --> 00:14:57.792
...it didn't feel like they were gone.

00:14:57.792 --> 00:15:01.958
This school is where the two of them are now--

00:15:01.958 --> 00:15:05.500
a place we can always return to.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:07.792
"Tea"

00:15:07.792 --> 00:15:12.208
We should think about putting this place
to some use, not just preserving it.

00:15:12.208 --> 00:15:14.875
You know--before we get busy with job-hunting.

00:15:14.875 --> 00:15:17.542
Okano's using the back of the mountain.

00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:21.208
She formed an acrobatic
performance squad at her sports college.

00:15:21.208 --> 00:15:24.708
Said this is the training field
she's most used to.

00:15:24.708 --> 00:15:28.167
We'll run the circuit! Follow me!

00:15:28.167 --> 00:15:31.292
Hup! Hup! C'mon! Faster!

00:15:31.292 --> 00:15:33.208
Whoa...

00:15:33.208 --> 00:15:37.708
And Kurahashi is giving nature tours to kids.

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:41.208
She's always had her ways
of earning pocket money.

00:15:41.208 --> 00:15:45.458
Okay, this way! Watch your step!

00:15:45.458 --> 00:15:47.667
Okay!

00:15:49.333 --> 00:15:53.917
We've all grown up
just as Koro Sensei taught us.

00:15:53.917 --> 00:15:56.083
Look at Manami and Takebayashi--

00:15:56.083 --> 00:16:00.625
taking hints from the activation cell
recipe in their advice books,

00:16:00.625 --> 00:16:02.875
they're researching an artificial
blood that can be transfused

00:16:02.875 --> 00:16:05.750
regardless of blood type.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:10.208
How many hundreds of millions
of people can be saved with this?

00:16:10.208 --> 00:16:13.250
Okuda did the bulk of development.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:16.875
I'd like to take it into
the clinical realm myself.

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:20.458
We call it "Rh slither blood."

00:16:21.375 --> 00:16:25.125
Sugino's become a college baseball ace.

00:16:32.083 --> 00:16:33.792
Strike three! Batter out!

00:16:33.792 --> 00:16:35.500
Yesss!

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:39.792
His versatile pitching has even
caught the eye of pro scouts.

00:16:39.792 --> 00:16:41.875
It slithers and curves even more than rumored!

00:16:41.875 --> 00:16:44.667
That Slithery Sugino is a tough one!

00:16:44.667 --> 00:16:47.000
Terasaka's strength and guts
have been recognized by

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:50.083
a certain professor politician.

00:16:50.083 --> 00:16:52.708
Hey! We'll be late for the lecture!

